Three clarifications:

DELTA_V_READ[3].3 reports current conductivity, not the retained AAH_200_AUX alarm. It becomes 1 when conductivity is acceptable. [3].12 reports the separate retained excess-drain alarm. Your table correctly distinguishes them.

The transition explanation still holds. If the chart evaluates “alarm clear,” an earlier clearance should satisfy that particular condition. Other conditions in the transition—or the chart being held—could still prevent advancement.

Restarting successfully does not, by itself, prove the fault is entirely inside DeltaV. The restart might reset chart state, reissue a command, or allow a remaining PLC condition to become satisfied.

